Calls through `#private` members lose `this` below ES2022 when the callee is parenthesized or has `!`, `as` or `satisfies`

> This issue was drafted with the help of LLMs (Claude and Codex); I reviewed it and verified the reproductions.

The tested TypeScript version is `7.1.0-dev.20261119.1` (`typescript@next` on November 20, 2026). `7.0.2` and `6.0.3` print the same, and the first four lines print `false` in every version I tried, back to `4.3.5`.

We ran into `(obj?.fn!)?.()` losing `this` while testing optional method calls in core-js, and checking which other callee shapes lose `this` in downlevel emit turned up calls through private members. The optional chaining shapes are reported in #65597.

Save as `repro.mts`:

```
class Example {
  #method(..._args: unknown[]) { return this; }

  run() {
    console.log((this.#method)() === this);
    console.log(this.#method!() === this);
    console.log((this.#method as any)() === this);
    console.log((this.#method)?.() === this);
    console.log(this.#method() === this);
    console.log(this.#method?.() === this);
[... 4 more lines]
```

```
npx --yes --package=typescript@7.1.0-dev.20261119.1 tsc --ignoreConfig --target es2021 --outDir out repro.mts
node out/repro.mjs
```

[Playground with TypeScript 6.0.3 and the ES2021 target](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?ts=6.0.3&target=8&strict=true#code/MYGwhgzhAECiAeYC2AHEBTaBvAUNaAxEugC4AWA9gCYAUAdAwPpgBOA5hAFzQCuAdgGs+FAO58A2gF0AlNmgtSPFn2jkAlhADc0AL4488-jVm58+YBT4QKGOiApsaNdRDpFSlKtOPQAvP9UyDWlNA3NLa1t7Rxc3YnJqAEIff19A4NCzaAsrG3Q7BydY9wSqaEhyvgBPb1lU9IgQsOyIvILHZyDXEs9pAH46FICXJqycyPzozo04j2ohtJHMs3G2qeL4zwGFhtHdHD0cPnQROERUDGM6FiMmoA)

**What actually happened**: The first four lines print `false`, so the method got `this === undefined`, and the last two print `true`. The first four calls are emitted without a receiver: `(__classPrivateFieldGet(this, _Example_instances, "m", _Example_method))()`, `__classPrivateFieldGet(this, _Example_instances, "m", _Example_method)()` for the `!` and `as` lines, and `(__classPrivateFieldGet(this, _Example_instances, "m", _Example_method))?.()`. The last two end in `.call(this)` and `?.call(this)`.

**What I expected**: All six lines print `true`, as they do with `node repro.mts` on Node.js 26.13.0 and with `--target es2022`. `!` and `as` are type-only, and a parenthesized private member access keeps its `this` when it is called.

The same happens with a tag, `` (this.#method)`x` ``, with `this.#method!?.()` and `(this.#method satisfies unknown)()`, and with other kinds of private members: a field holding a function, `(this.#field)()`, a getter returning one, `(this.#getter)()`, and a static method, `(Example.#staticMethod)()`.

