```

```
bar("x");
/** leading comment */
foo();
```

Synthesized nodes (`pos === -1`) shouldn't pick up comments from the original source text.

The cause appears to be in `dist/api/node/encoder.js`, `encodeNode`:

```
nodeValues.push(node.kind, node.pos >= 0 ? node.pos : 0, node.end >= 0 ? node.end : 0, ...)
```

The same clamping happens for the root node and for node lists. The Go side then receives synthesized nodes with range `[0, 0]`. It can't tell them apart from real nodes at the start of the file, so it emits the leading comments at position 0 for each of them.

Workaround: print the statements inside a new source file with empty text (`createSourceFile(statements, eof, "", fileName, path)`). This avoids the duplicates but also drops all original comments, which isn't acceptable for codegen that must keep JSDoc or `/* @__PURE__ */` annotations.

