```

When downleveling the `static {}` block (`target <= es2021`), tsgo rewrites `this.bar()` inside the regular `function` expression to `_a.bar()`:

```
var _a;
export class Foo {
    bar() {
        return 1;
    }
}
_a = Foo;
(() => {
    _a;
    _a.prototype.toObject = function () {
[... 3 more lines]
```

At runtime, calling `new Foo().toObject()` throws `TypeError: _a.bar is not a function` because `_a` is the class constructor `Foo`, not the instance receiver `this`.

`this.bar()` inside the regular `function` expression is preserved, as tsc 6.0.3 emits:

```
var _a;
export class Foo {
    bar() {
        return 1;
    }
}
_a = Foo;
(() => {
    _a;
    _a.prototype.toObject = function () {
[... 3 more lines]
```

In [`tsc/internal/transformers/estransforms/classfields.go`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/aa8149273b23401f0a79a5f0384c42de51888693/tsc/internal/transformers/estransforms/classfields.go#L265-L273):

1. When a class has a constructor alias in `tx.classAliases` (`_a = Foo`) and `classFieldsTransformer` transforms a `static {}` block, `tx.currentClassElement` is set to the `ClassStaticBlockDeclaration`.
2. Inside the `static {}` block, a regular `FunctionExpression` masks out `SubtreeContainsLexicalThis | SubtreeContainsLexicalSuper` via `^SubtreeExclusionsFunction`.
3. When `visit` visits the `Foo.prototype.toObject = function () { ... }` statement (or the `FunctionExpression` itself), `node.SubtreeFacts() & (ast.SubtreeContainsClassFields | ast.SubtreeContainsLexicalThisOrSuper) == 0` while `len(tx.classAliases) > 0`, so `visit` delegates to `tx.visitForSubstitution(node)` without passing through `visitFunctionExpressionOrDeclaration` (leaving `tx.currentClassElement` set to the enclosing static block).
4. Inside `visitForSubstitution`, `tx.substitutionVisitor` traverses into the function body and encounters `this.bar`. Because `this.bar` is a `PropertyAccessExpression` whose `.Name()` is an identifier, `visitForSubstitution` calls `visitPropertyAccessExpressionForSubstitution`.
5. `visitPropertyAccessExpressionForSubstitution` (added in microsoft/typescript-go#3147, dd25debd25) visits `node.Expression` with `tx.Visitor()` (the full `tx.visit` visitor) instead of the active visitor (`tx.substitutionVisitor` when called from `visitForSubstitution`).
6. Because the `ThisKeyword` node itself has `SubtreeContainsLexicalThis`, `tx.visit(this)` dispatches to `visitThisExpression`, sees `tx.currentClassElement` is still the static block, and replaces `this` with `_a`.

Passing the active visitor into `visitPropertyAccessExpressionForSubstitution` (`tx.substitutionVisitor` from `visitForSubstitution`, `tx.Visitor()` from `visitPropertyAccessExpression`) fixes the issue:

```
--- a/tsc/internal/transformers/estransforms/classfields.go
+++ b/tsc/internal/transformers/estransforms/classfields.go
@@ -268,7 +268,7 @@ func (tx *classFieldsTransformer) visitForSubstitution(node *ast.Node) *ast.Node
 		return tx.visitIdentifier(node.AsIdentifier())
 	}
 	if node.Kind == ast.KindPropertyAccessExpression && ast.IsIdentifier(node.AsPropertyAccessExpression().Name()) {
-		return tx.visitPropertyAccessExpressionForSubstitution(node.AsPropertyAccessExpression())
+		return tx.visitPropertyAccessExpressionForSubstitution(node.AsPropertyAccessExpression(), tx.substitutionVisitor)
 	}
 	return tx.substitutionVisitor.VisitEachChild(node)
